            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-10536",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl: libcurl: Use-after-free vulnerability leading to Denial of Service"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application\nconfigures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or\n`CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and\nfinally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final\ncleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure\nthat was already freed during the reset operation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-10536",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-10536](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-10536)\nA use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application\nconfigures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or\n`CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and\nfinally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final\ncleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure\nthat was already freed during the reset operation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libcurl4t64||[CVE-2026-10536](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-10536)|\n\nA use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application\nconfigures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or\n`CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and\nfinally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final\ncleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure\nthat was already freed during the reset operation."
              },
              "properties": {
