            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82208",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "curl: libcurl: Improper certificate validation when using wolfSSL CA cache"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "With the wolfSSL backend, when CA caching is enabled and an\n`CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION` callback replaces the trust store, libcurl can\nsilently reinstall the cached store after the callback returns. A certificate\ntrusted by the cached store but rejected by the callback-selected store is\nthen incorrectly accepted."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82208",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82208\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-82208](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82208)\nWith the wolfSSL backend, when CA caching is enabled and an\n`CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION` callback replaces the trust store, libcurl can\nsilently reinstall the cached store after the callback returns. A certificate\ntrusted by the cached store but rejected by the callback-selected store is\nthen incorrectly accepted.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82208**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libcurl4t64||[CVE-2026-82208](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82208)|\n\nWith the wolfSSL backend, when CA caching is enabled and an\n`CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION` callback replaces the trust store, libcurl can\nsilently reinstall the cached store after the callback returns. A certificate\ntrusted by the cached store but rejected by the callback-selected store is\nthen incorrectly accepted."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82209",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "curl: libcurl: Information disclosure via improper Public Suffix List boundary check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82209",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-82209](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82209)\nWhen libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libcurl4t64||[CVE-2026-82209](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82209)|\n\nWhen libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
