                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93990**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|libexpat1||[CVE-2026-93990](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93990)|\n\nExpat before 2.8.5 fails to validate that a high surrogate in UTF-16 input is followed by a low surrogate, allowing malformed UTF-16 sequences to be accepted. Attackers can supply UTF-16 encoded XML containing lone high surrogates that consume the following code unit, causing Expat to pass unpaired surrogates to applications built with XML_UNICODE and to silently replace input characters in other builds."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
