            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-39762",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amd/display: add null check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: add null check\n\n[WHY]\nPrevents null pointer dereferences to enhance function robustness\n\n[HOW]\nAdds early null check and return false if invalid."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39762",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-39762\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-39762](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39762)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: add null check\n\n[WHY]\nPrevents null pointer dereferences to enhance function robustness\n\n[HOW]\nAdds early null check and return false if invalid.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-39762**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-39762](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39762)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: add null check\n\n[WHY]\nPrevents null pointer dereferences to enhance function robustness\n\n[HOW]\nAdds early null check and return false if invalid."
              },
