            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-39834",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net/mlx5: HWS, Fix memory leak in hws_action_get_shared_stc_nic error flow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: HWS, Fix memory leak in hws_action_get_shared_stc_nic error flow\n\nWhen an invalid stc_type is provided, the function allocates memory for\nshared_stc but jumps to unlock_and_out without freeing it, causing a\nmemory leak.\n\nFix by jumping to free_shared_stc label instead to ensure proper cleanup."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39834",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-39834\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-39834](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39834)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: HWS, Fix memory leak in hws_action_get_shared_stc_nic error flow\n\nWhen an invalid stc_type is provided, the function allocates memory for\nshared_stc but jumps to unlock_and_out without freeing it, causing a\nmemory leak.\n\nFix by jumping to free_shared_stc label instead to ensure proper cleanup.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-39834**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-39834](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39834)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: HWS, Fix memory leak in hws_action_get_shared_stc_nic error flow\n\nWhen an invalid stc_type is provided, the function allocates memory for\nshared_stc but jumps to unlock_and_out without freeing it, causing a\nmemory leak.\n\nFix by jumping to free_shared_stc label instead to ensure proper cleanup."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
