            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-71188",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: dmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken when looking up the DMA mux\nplatform device during route allocation.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away so there is no point in keeping the reference."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71188",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-71188\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-71188](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71188)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken when looking up the DMA mux\nplatform device during route allocation.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away so there is no point in keeping the reference.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-71188**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-71188](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71188)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken when looking up the DMA mux\nplatform device during route allocation.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away so there is no point in keeping the reference."
