              "id": "CVE-2026-100074",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  b ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark bpf_refcount field as unique\n\nBPF_REFCOUNT is not marked as a unique field, while it should be. Fix\nthis oversight."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-100074",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-100074\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-100074](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-100074)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark bpf_refcount field as unique\n\nBPF_REFCOUNT is not marked as a unique field, while it should be. Fix\nthis oversight.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-100074**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-100074](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-100074)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark bpf_refcount field as unique\n\nBPF_REFCOUNT is not marked as a unique field, while it should be. Fix\nthis oversight."
              },
