            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43022",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Bluetooth: hci_sync: hci_cmd_sync_queue_once() return -EEXIST if exists"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_sync: hci_cmd_sync_queue_once() return -EEXIST if exists\n\nhci_cmd_sync_queue_once() needs to indicate whether a queue item was\nadded, so caller can know if callbacks are called, so it can avoid\nleaking resources.\n\nChange the function to return -EEXIST if queue item already exists.\n\nModify all callsites to handle that."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43022",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43022\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-43022](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43022)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_sync: hci_cmd_sync_queue_once() return -EEXIST if exists\n\nhci_cmd_sync_queue_once() needs to indicate whether a queue item was\nadded, so caller can know if callbacks are called, so it can avoid\nleaking resources.\n\nChange the function to return -EEXIST if queue item already exists.\n\nModify all callsites to handle that.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43022**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-43022](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43022)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_sync: hci_cmd_sync_queue_once() return -EEXIST if exists\n\nhci_cmd_sync_queue_once() needs to indicate whether a queue item was\nadded, so caller can know if callbacks are called, so it can avoid\nleaking resources.\n\nChange the function to return -EEXIST if queue item already exists.\n\nModify all callsites to handle that."
              },
