            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43127",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ntfs3: fix circular locking dependency in run_unpack_ex"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs3: fix circular locking dependency in run_unpack_ex\n\nSyzbot reported a circular locking dependency between wnd-\u003erw_lock\n(sbi-\u003eused.bitmap) and ni-\u003efile.run_lock.\n\nThe deadlock scenario:\n1. ntfs_extend_mft() takes ni-\u003efile.run_lock then wnd-\u003erw_lock.\n2. run_unpack_ex() takes wnd-\u003erw_lock then tries to acquire\n   ni-\u003efile.run_lock inside ntfs_refresh_zone().\n\nThis creates an AB-BA deadlock.\n\nFix this by using down_read_trylock() instead of down_read() when\nacquiring run_lock in run_unpack_ex(). If the lock is contended,\nskip ntfs_refresh_zone() - the MFT zone will be refreshed on the\nnext MFT operation. This breaks the circular dependency since we\nnever block waiting for run_lock while holding wnd-\u003erw_lock."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43127",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43127\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-43127](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43127)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs3: fix circular locking dependency in run_unpack_ex\n\nSyzbot reported a circular locking dependency between wnd-\u003erw_lock\n(sbi-\u003eused.bitmap) and ni-\u003efile.run_lock.\n\nThe deadlock scenario:\n1. ntfs_extend_mft() takes ni-\u003efile.run_lock then wnd-\u003erw_lock.\n2. run_unpack_ex() takes wnd-\u003erw_lock then tries to acquire\n   ni-\u003efile.run_lock inside ntfs_refresh_zone().\n\nThis creates an AB-BA deadlock.\n\nFix this by using down_read_trylock() instead of down_read() when\nacquiring run_lock in run_unpack_ex(). If the lock is contended,\nskip ntfs_refresh_zone() - the MFT zone will be refreshed on the\nnext MFT operation. This breaks the circular dependency since we\nnever block waiting for run_lock while holding wnd-\u003erw_lock.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43127**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-43127](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43127)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs3: fix circular locking dependency in run_unpack_ex\n\nSyzbot reported a circular locking dependency between wnd-\u003erw_lock\n(sbi-\u003eused.bitmap) and ni-\u003efile.run_lock.\n\nThe deadlock scenario:\n1. ntfs_extend_mft() takes ni-\u003efile.run_lock then wnd-\u003erw_lock.\n2. run_unpack_ex() takes wnd-\u003erw_lock then tries to acquire\n   ni-\u003efile.run_lock inside ntfs_refresh_zone().\n\nThis creates an AB-BA deadlock.\n\nFix this by using down_read_trylock() instead of down_read() when\nacquiring run_lock in run_unpack_ex(). If the lock is contended,\nskip ntfs_refresh_zone() - the MFT zone will be refreshed on the\nnext MFT operation. This breaks the circular dependency since we\nnever block waiting for run_lock while holding wnd-\u003erw_lock."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
