            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43172",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: iwlwifi: fix 22000 series SMEM parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: fix 22000 series SMEM parsing\n\nIf the firmware were to report three LMACs (which doesn't\nexist in hardware) then using \"fwrt-\u003esmem_cfg.lmac[2]\" is\nan overrun of the array. Reject such and use IWL_FW_CHECK\ninstead of WARN_ON in this function."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43172",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43172\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-43172](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43172)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: fix 22000 series SMEM parsing\n\nIf the firmware were to report three LMACs (which doesn't\nexist in hardware) then using \"fwrt-\u003esmem_cfg.lmac[2]\" is\nan overrun of the array. Reject such and use IWL_FW_CHECK\ninstead of WARN_ON in this function.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43172**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-43172](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43172)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: fix 22000 series SMEM parsing\n\nIf the firmware were to report three LMACs (which doesn't\nexist in hardware) then using \"fwrt-\u003esmem_cfg.lmac[2]\" is\nan overrun of the array. Reject such and use IWL_FW_CHECK\ninstead of WARN_ON in this function."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
