            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43301",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: media: chips-media: wave5: Fix PM runtime usage count underflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: chips-media: wave5: Fix PM runtime usage count underflow\n\nReplace pm_runtime_put_sync() with pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() in\nthe remove path to properly pair with pm_runtime_use_autosuspend() from\nprobe. This allows pm_runtime_disable() to handle reference count cleanup\ncorrectly regardless of current suspend state.\n\nThe driver calls pm_runtime_put_sync() unconditionally in remove, but the\ndevice may already be suspended due to autosuspend configured in probe.\nWhen autosuspend has already suspended the device, the usage count is 0,\nand pm_runtime_put_sync() decrements it to -1.\n\nThis causes the following warning on module unload:\n\n  ------------[ cut here ]------------\n  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 963 at kernel/kthread.c:1430\n    kthread_destroy_worker+0x84/0x98\n  ...\n  vdec 30210000.video-codec: Runtime PM usage count underflow!"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43301",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43301\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-43301](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43301)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: chips-media: wave5: Fix PM runtime usage count underflow\n\nReplace pm_runtime_put_sync() with pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() in\nthe remove path to properly pair with pm_runtime_use_autosuspend() from\nprobe. This allows pm_runtime_disable() to handle reference count cleanup\ncorrectly regardless of current suspend state.\n\nThe driver calls pm_runtime_put_sync() unconditionally in remove, but the\ndevice may already be suspended due to autosuspend configured in probe.\nWhen autosuspend has already suspended the device, the usage count is 0,\nand pm_runtime_put_sync() decrements it to -1.\n\nThis causes the following warning on module unload:\n\n  ------------[ cut here ]------------\n  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 963 at kernel/kthread.c:1430\n    kthread_destroy_worker+0x84/0x98\n  ...\n  vdec 30210000.video-codec: Runtime PM usage count underflow!",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43301**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-43301](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43301)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: chips-media: wave5: Fix PM runtime usage count underflow\n\nReplace pm_runtime_put_sync() with pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() in\nthe remove path to properly pair with pm_runtime_use_autosuspend() from\nprobe. This allows pm_runtime_disable() to handle reference count cleanup\ncorrectly regardless of current suspend state.\n\nThe driver calls pm_runtime_put_sync() unconditionally in remove, but the\ndevice may already be suspended due to autosuspend configured in probe.\nWhen autosuspend has already suspended the device, the usage count is 0,\nand pm_runtime_put_sync() decrements it to -1.\n\nThis causes the following warning on module unload:\n\n  ------------[ cut here ]------------\n  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 963 at kernel/kthread.c:1430\n    kthread_destroy_worker+0x84/0x98\n  ...\n  vdec 30210000.video-codec: Runtime PM usage count underflow!"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43308",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: btrfs: don't BUG() on unexpected delayed ref type in run_one_delayed_ref()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: don't BUG() on unexpected delayed ref type in run_one_delayed_ref()\n\nThere is no need to BUG(), we can just return an error and log an error\nmessage."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43308",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43308\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-43308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43308)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: don't BUG() on unexpected delayed ref type in run_one_delayed_ref()\n\nThere is no need to BUG(), we can just return an error and log an error\nmessage.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43308**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-43308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43308)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: don't BUG() on unexpected delayed ref type in run_one_delayed_ref()\n\nThere is no need to BUG(), we can just return an error and log an error\nmessage."
