            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-52983",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net: airoha: fix BQL imbalance in TX path"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: airoha: fix BQL imbalance in TX path\n\nFix a possible BQL imbalance in airoha_dev_xmit(), where inflight\npackets are accounted only for the AIROHA_NUM_TX_RING netdev TX\nqueues. The queue index is computed as:\n\n    qid = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) % ARRAY_SIZE(qdma-\u003eq_tx)\n    txq = netdev_get_tx_queue(dev, qid);\n\nHowever, airoha_qdma_tx_napi_poll() accounts completions across all\nnetdev TX queues (num_tx_queues), leading to inconsistent BQL\naccounting.\n\nAlso reset all netdev TX queues in the ndo_stop callback."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-52983",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-52983\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-52983](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-52983)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: airoha: fix BQL imbalance in TX path\n\nFix a possible BQL imbalance in airoha_dev_xmit(), where inflight\npackets are accounted only for the AIROHA_NUM_TX_RING netdev TX\nqueues. The queue index is computed as:\n\n    qid = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) % ARRAY_SIZE(qdma-\u003eq_tx)\n    txq = netdev_get_tx_queue(dev, qid);\n\nHowever, airoha_qdma_tx_napi_poll() accounts completions across all\nnetdev TX queues (num_tx_queues), leading to inconsistent BQL\naccounting.\n\nAlso reset all netdev TX queues in the ndo_stop callback.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-52983**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-52983](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-52983)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: airoha: fix BQL imbalance in TX path\n\nFix a possible BQL imbalance in airoha_dev_xmit(), where inflight\npackets are accounted only for the AIROHA_NUM_TX_RING netdev TX\nqueues. The queue index is computed as:\n\n    qid = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) % ARRAY_SIZE(qdma-\u003eq_tx)\n    txq = netdev_get_tx_queue(dev, qid);\n\nHowever, airoha_qdma_tx_napi_poll() accounts completions across all\nnetdev TX queues (num_tx_queues), leading to inconsistent BQL\naccounting.\n\nAlso reset all netdev TX queues in the ndo_stop callback."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
