            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64154",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/msm/adreno: Fix a reference leak in a6xx_gpu_init()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/adreno: Fix a reference leak in a6xx_gpu_init()\n\nIn a6xx_gpu_init(), node is obtained via of_parse_phandle().\nWhile there was a manual of_node_put() at the end of the\ncommon path, several early error returns would bypass this call,\nresulting in a reference leak.\nFix this by using the __free(device_node) cleanup handler to\nrelease the reference when the variable goes out of scope.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/700661/"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64154",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64154\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64154](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64154)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/adreno: Fix a reference leak in a6xx_gpu_init()\n\nIn a6xx_gpu_init(), node is obtained via of_parse_phandle().\nWhile there was a manual of_node_put() at the end of the\ncommon path, several early error returns would bypass this call,\nresulting in a reference leak.\nFix this by using the __free(device_node) cleanup handler to\nrelease the reference when the variable goes out of scope.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/700661/",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64154**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64154](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64154)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/adreno: Fix a reference leak in a6xx_gpu_init()\n\nIn a6xx_gpu_init(), node is obtained via of_parse_phandle().\nWhile there was a manual of_node_put() at the end of the\ncommon path, several early error returns would bypass this call,\nresulting in a reference leak.\nFix this by using the __free(device_node) cleanup handler to\nrelease the reference when the variable goes out of scope.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/700661/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
