            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64212",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: iwlwifi: mld: don't dereference a pointer before NULL checking it"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: don't dereference a pointer before NULL checking it\n\nIn iwl_mld_remove_link, the link-\u003efw_id is saved at the beginning of the\nfunction so we have it after we freed the link.\n\nBut the link pointer can be NULL, and is not checked when the fw_id is\nstored.\n\nFix it by simply freeing the link at the end of the function.\n\nfFixes: 0e66a39f4f0e (\"wifi: iwlwifi: fix potential use after free in iwl_mld_remove_link()\")"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64212",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64212\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64212](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64212)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: don't dereference a pointer before NULL checking it\n\nIn iwl_mld_remove_link, the link-\u003efw_id is saved at the beginning of the\nfunction so we have it after we freed the link.\n\nBut the link pointer can be NULL, and is not checked when the fw_id is\nstored.\n\nFix it by simply freeing the link at the end of the function.\n\nfFixes: 0e66a39f4f0e (\"wifi: iwlwifi: fix potential use after free in iwl_mld_remove_link()\")",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64212**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64212](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64212)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: don't dereference a pointer before NULL checking it\n\nIn iwl_mld_remove_link, the link-\u003efw_id is saved at the beginning of the\nfunction so we have it after we freed the link.\n\nBut the link pointer can be NULL, and is not checked when the fw_id is\nstored.\n\nFix it by simply freeing the link at the end of the function.\n\nfFixes: 0e66a39f4f0e (\"wifi: iwlwifi: fix potential use after free in iwl_mld_remove_link()\")"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
