            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64255",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers\n\nThree BA session handlers use ffs(ba_data-\u003esta_mask) - 1 to derive a\nstation ID without checking that sta_mask is non-zero. When sta_mask is\nzero, ffs() returns 0 and the subtraction wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing\nan out-of-bounds access on fw_id_to_link_sta[].\n\nAdd WARN_ON_ONCE(!ba_data-\u003esta_mask) guards before each ffs() call,\nconsistent with the existing check in iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64255",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64255\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64255](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64255)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers\n\nThree BA session handlers use ffs(ba_data-\u003esta_mask) - 1 to derive a\nstation ID without checking that sta_mask is non-zero. When sta_mask is\nzero, ffs() returns 0 and the subtraction wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing\nan out-of-bounds access on fw_id_to_link_sta[].\n\nAdd WARN_ON_ONCE(!ba_data-\u003esta_mask) guards before each ffs() call,\nconsistent with the existing check in iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64255**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64255](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64255)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers\n\nThree BA session handlers use ffs(ba_data-\u003esta_mask) - 1 to derive a\nstation ID without checking that sta_mask is non-zero. When sta_mask is\nzero, ffs() returns 0 and the subtraction wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing\nan out-of-bounds access on fw_id_to_link_sta[].\n\nAdd WARN_ON_ONCE(!ba_data-\u003esta_mask) guards before each ffs() call,\nconsistent with the existing check in iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
