            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68233",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/vc4: Shut down BO cache timer before teardown"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vc4: Shut down BO cache timer before teardown\n\nThe BO cache timer callback schedules time_work, and time_work can rearm\nthe timer through vc4_bo_cache_free_old().\n\nvc4_bo_cache_destroy() deletes the timer and then cancels the work, which\ndoes not break that cycle: the work being cancelled can rearm the timer,\nand the timer then queues work again after teardown.\n\nUse timer_shutdown_sync() instead, so the timer cannot be rearmed and the\ncycle ends with cancel_work_sync()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68233",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68233\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-68233](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68233)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vc4: Shut down BO cache timer before teardown\n\nThe BO cache timer callback schedules time_work, and time_work can rearm\nthe timer through vc4_bo_cache_free_old().\n\nvc4_bo_cache_destroy() deletes the timer and then cancels the work, which\ndoes not break that cycle: the work being cancelled can rearm the timer,\nand the timer then queues work again after teardown.\n\nUse timer_shutdown_sync() instead, so the timer cannot be rearmed and the\ncycle ends with cancel_work_sync().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68233**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-68233](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68233)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vc4: Shut down BO cache timer before teardown\n\nThe BO cache timer callback schedules time_work, and time_work can rearm\nthe timer through vc4_bo_cache_free_old().\n\nvc4_bo_cache_destroy() deletes the timer and then cancels the work, which\ndoes not break that cycle: the work being cancelled can rearm the timer,\nand the timer then queues work again after teardown.\n\nUse timer_shutdown_sync() instead, so the timer cannot be rearmed and the\ncycle ends with cancel_work_sync()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68242",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure\n\nAvoid using intel_context_put() before intel_context_init() in\nexeclists_create_virtual() as the kref_put() inside would lead\nto NULL deref on the IOCTL path when sched_engine allocation fails.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by\nIntel Product Security.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f2a12f2d50e9f48227656e4dcbd6423506be31d)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68242",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68242\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-68242](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68242)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure\n\nAvoid using intel_context_put() before intel_context_init() in\nexeclists_create_virtual() as the kref_put() inside would lead\nto NULL deref on the IOCTL path when sched_engine allocation fails.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by\nIntel Product Security.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f2a12f2d50e9f48227656e4dcbd6423506be31d)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68242**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-68242](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68242)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure\n\nAvoid using intel_context_put() before intel_context_init() in\nexeclists_create_virtual() as the kref_put() inside would lead\nto NULL deref on the IOCTL path when sched_engine allocation fails.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by\nIntel Product Security.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f2a12f2d50e9f48227656e4dcbd6423506be31d)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68258",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size\n\nWe weren't checking whether the values provided in the private\ndata in kfd CRIU restore were within bounds.\n\nFor queue type, add a KFD_QUEUE_TYPE_MAX and ensure the provided\ntype is less than it.\n\nFor mqd_size, add new function mqd_size_from_queue_type and confirm\nthat the provided mqd_size matches expectations.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f19d8086f6644083c913d70bfdeee20e1b6f46a5)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68258",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68258\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-68258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68258)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size\n\nWe weren't checking whether the values provided in the private\ndata in kfd CRIU restore were within bounds.\n\nFor queue type, add a KFD_QUEUE_TYPE_MAX and ensure the provided\ntype is less than it.\n\nFor mqd_size, add new function mqd_size_from_queue_type and confirm\nthat the provided mqd_size matches expectations.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f19d8086f6644083c913d70bfdeee20e1b6f46a5)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68258**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-68258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68258)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size\n\nWe weren't checking whether the values provided in the private\ndata in kfd CRIU restore were within bounds.\n\nFor queue type, add a KFD_QUEUE_TYPE_MAX and ensure the provided\ntype is less than it.\n\nFor mqd_size, add new function mqd_size_from_queue_type and confirm\nthat the provided mqd_size matches expectations.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f19d8086f6644083c913d70bfdeee20e1b6f46a5)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
