            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-72397",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: hwmon: (pmbus/core) honor vrm_version in pmbus_data2reg_vid()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: (pmbus/core) honor vrm_version in pmbus_data2reg_vid()\n\npmbus_data2reg_vid() hardcoded the VR11 encoding regardless of the\nvrm_version configured by the driver, while pmbus_reg2data_vid()\nalready switched on it. Any driver that selects a non-VR11 VID mode\nand exposes a regulator (or hwmon vout setter) sent dangerously\nwrong codes to PMBUS_VOUT_COMMAND -- e.g. an nvidia195mv part asked\nfor 200 mV got the VR11 clamp to 500 mV encoded as 0xB2, which the\nchip interprets as 1080 mV.\n\nMirror pmbus_reg2data_vid() so writes round-trip with reads."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72397",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-72397\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-72397](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72397)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: (pmbus/core) honor vrm_version in pmbus_data2reg_vid()\n\npmbus_data2reg_vid() hardcoded the VR11 encoding regardless of the\nvrm_version configured by the driver, while pmbus_reg2data_vid()\nalready switched on it. Any driver that selects a non-VR11 VID mode\nand exposes a regulator (or hwmon vout setter) sent dangerously\nwrong codes to PMBUS_VOUT_COMMAND -- e.g. an nvidia195mv part asked\nfor 200 mV got the VR11 clamp to 500 mV encoded as 0xB2, which the\nchip interprets as 1080 mV.\n\nMirror pmbus_reg2data_vid() so writes round-trip with reads.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-72397**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-72397](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72397)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: (pmbus/core) honor vrm_version in pmbus_data2reg_vid()\n\npmbus_data2reg_vid() hardcoded the VR11 encoding regardless of the\nvrm_version configured by the driver, while pmbus_reg2data_vid()\nalready switched on it. Any driver that selects a non-VR11 VID mode\nand exposes a regulator (or hwmon vout setter) sent dangerously\nwrong codes to PMBUS_VOUT_COMMAND -- e.g. an nvidia195mv part asked\nfor 200 mV got the VR11 clamp to 500 mV encoded as 0xB2, which the\nchip interprets as 1080 mV.\n\nMirror pmbus_reg2data_vid() so writes round-trip with reads."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
