            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89437",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: platform/x86: int1092: Fix potential memory leak in sar_probe()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: int1092: Fix potential memory leak in sar_probe()\n\nThe memory allocated for device_mode_info in parse_package() called by\nsar_get_data() is not freed in some of the error paths in sar_probe().\nFix that by converting to use device managed allocations."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89437",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89437\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89437](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89437)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: int1092: Fix potential memory leak in sar_probe()\n\nThe memory allocated for device_mode_info in parse_package() called by\nsar_get_data() is not freed in some of the error paths in sar_probe().\nFix that by converting to use device managed allocations.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89437**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89437](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89437)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: int1092: Fix potential memory leak in sar_probe()\n\nThe memory allocated for device_mode_info in parse_package() called by\nsar_get_data() is not freed in some of the error paths in sar_probe().\nFix that by converting to use device managed allocations."
