            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90023",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  u ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_mass_storage: fix null pointer dereference in fsg_common_set_num_buffers()\n\nPreviously fsg_num_buffers_validate() was removed as it was not\nnecessary due to Kconfig setting the limits for n from 2 to 256 with\ndefault as 2. However, setting the page content in such a way that\nkstrtou8() reflects n value as either 0 or 1 bypasses these\nrestrictions leading to a null pointer dereference if n is 0. Fix\nthis by adding a check for n \u003c 2 and returning -EINVAL if n is\neither 0 or 1 consistent with Kconfig logic."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90023",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90023\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90023](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90023)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_mass_storage: fix null pointer dereference in fsg_common_set_num_buffers()\n\nPreviously fsg_num_buffers_validate() was removed as it was not\nnecessary due to Kconfig setting the limits for n from 2 to 256 with\ndefault as 2. However, setting the page content in such a way that\nkstrtou8() reflects n value as either 0 or 1 bypasses these\nrestrictions leading to a null pointer dereference if n is 0. Fix\nthis by adding a check for n \u003c 2 and returning -EINVAL if n is\neither 0 or 1 consistent with Kconfig logic.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90023**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90023](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90023)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_mass_storage: fix null pointer dereference in fsg_common_set_num_buffers()\n\nPreviously fsg_num_buffers_validate() was removed as it was not\nnecessary due to Kconfig setting the limits for n from 2 to 256 with\ndefault as 2. However, setting the page content in such a way that\nkstrtou8() reflects n value as either 0 or 1 bypasses these\nrestrictions leading to a null pointer dereference if n is 0. Fix\nthis by adding a check for n \u003c 2 and returning -EINVAL if n is\neither 0 or 1 consistent with Kconfig logic."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
