            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90106",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  n ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: arp/nd proxy: fix reading neigh ha\n\nCurrently neigh ha address is read directly, but that can result in\ntorn/partial reads if the neigh is being updated. Use neigh_ha_snapshot\nto take a stable snapshot of the address."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90106",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90106\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90106](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90106)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: arp/nd proxy: fix reading neigh ha\n\nCurrently neigh ha address is read directly, but that can result in\ntorn/partial reads if the neigh is being updated. Use neigh_ha_snapshot\nto take a stable snapshot of the address.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90106**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90106](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90106)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: arp/nd proxy: fix reading neigh ha\n\nCurrently neigh ha address is read directly, but that can result in\ntorn/partial reads if the neigh is being updated. Use neigh_ha_snapshot\nto take a stable snapshot of the address."
