            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90217",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  b ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Compare iterator types during state pruning\n\nAn iterator stack slot can be MEM_RCU or PTR_UNTRUSTED. These states\nmust not be equal, or the verifier can prune an unsafe path.\n\nCompare the pointer type for STACK_ITER slots."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90217",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90217\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90217](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90217)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Compare iterator types during state pruning\n\nAn iterator stack slot can be MEM_RCU or PTR_UNTRUSTED. These states\nmust not be equal, or the verifier can prune an unsafe path.\n\nCompare the pointer type for STACK_ITER slots.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90217**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90217](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90217)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Compare iterator types during state pruning\n\nAn iterator stack slot can be MEM_RCU or PTR_UNTRUSTED. These states\nmust not be equal, or the verifier can prune an unsafe path.\n\nCompare the pointer type for STACK_ITER slots."
