            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90259",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  b ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: qgroup: fix a wrong length calculation in qgroup_free_reserved_data()\n\nIn that function, we round down the start position and round up the\nending position.\n\nBut during the calculation of @len, we use \"round_up(start + len,\nsectorsize)\", which is the rounded up end position, not the rounded up\nlength.\n\nWhich results a much larger length, and later we are still using\n\"start + len\", which is completely incorrect.\n\nFix it by declaring a local @aligned_start and @aligned_len and use them\ninstead."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90259",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90259\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90259](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90259)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: qgroup: fix a wrong length calculation in qgroup_free_reserved_data()\n\nIn that function, we round down the start position and round up the\nending position.\n\nBut during the calculation of @len, we use \"round_up(start + len,\nsectorsize)\", which is the rounded up end position, not the rounded up\nlength.\n\nWhich results a much larger length, and later we are still using\n\"start + len\", which is completely incorrect.\n\nFix it by declaring a local @aligned_start and @aligned_len and use them\ninstead.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90259**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90259](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90259)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: qgroup: fix a wrong length calculation in qgroup_free_reserved_data()\n\nIn that function, we round down the start position and round up the\nending position.\n\nBut during the calculation of @len, we use \"round_up(start + len,\nsectorsize)\", which is the rounded up end position, not the rounded up\nlength.\n\nWhich results a much larger length, and later we are still using\n\"start + len\", which is completely incorrect.\n\nFix it by declaring a local @aligned_start and @aligned_len and use them\ninstead."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
