            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90335",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  t ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: skip cdev_del() when no cdev is registered\n\nTTY device registration can fail before a cdev is allocated.\nSerial core keeps the port so setserial can still use it, and later\nremoval passes the NULL cdev slot to cdev_del(), causing a NULL-pointer\ndereference.\n\nOnly delete the cdev when the slot is not NULL."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90335",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90335\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90335](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90335)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: skip cdev_del() when no cdev is registered\n\nTTY device registration can fail before a cdev is allocated.\nSerial core keeps the port so setserial can still use it, and later\nremoval passes the NULL cdev slot to cdev_del(), causing a NULL-pointer\ndereference.\n\nOnly delete the cdev when the slot is not NULL.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90335**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90335](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90335)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: skip cdev_del() when no cdev is registered\n\nTTY device registration can fail before a cdev is allocated.\nSerial core keeps the port so setserial can still use it, and later\nremoval passes the NULL cdev slot to cdev_del(), causing a NULL-pointer\ndereference.\n\nOnly delete the cdev when the slot is not NULL."
              },
