            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90365",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: cancel reset and rc work on device unregister\n\nBoth drivers cancelled dump_work on unregister but left reset_work and\nrc_work to be flushed only by destroy_workqueue() in mt76_free_device(),\nwhich runs after the hw is unregistered and the hardware stopped. A\nreset_work that fires in that window calls ieee80211_restart_hw() and\nre-arms mac_work on an unregistered hw, and rc_work touches station state\nbeing torn down. Cancel both up front, alongside dump_work."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90365",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90365\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90365](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90365)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: cancel reset and rc work on device unregister\n\nBoth drivers cancelled dump_work on unregister but left reset_work and\nrc_work to be flushed only by destroy_workqueue() in mt76_free_device(),\nwhich runs after the hw is unregistered and the hardware stopped. A\nreset_work that fires in that window calls ieee80211_restart_hw() and\nre-arms mac_work on an unregistered hw, and rc_work touches station state\nbeing torn down. Cancel both up front, alongside dump_work.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90365**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90365](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90365)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: cancel reset and rc work on device unregister\n\nBoth drivers cancelled dump_work on unregister but left reset_work and\nrc_work to be flushed only by destroy_workqueue() in mt76_free_device(),\nwhich runs after the hw is unregistered and the hardware stopped. A\nreset_work that fires in that window calls ieee80211_restart_hw() and\nre-arms mac_work on an unregistered hw, and rc_work touches station state\nbeing torn down. Cancel both up front, alongside dump_work."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90367",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: hold dev-\u003emt76.mutex while disabling tx worker in SER\n\nmt7996_mac_reset_work() parked the tx worker and disabled the RX/TX NAPIs\nbefore taking dev-\u003emt76.mutex. mt76_worker_disable()/_enable() are plain\nkthread park/unpark, not refcounted, and __mt76_set_channel() toggles the\nsame worker and the MT76_RESET bit under the mutex. An L1 SER racing a\nchannel switch could therefore have the worker unparked and MT76_RESET\ncleared while the reset path resets the DMA rings, corrupting descriptors\nor tokens. Take the mutex before disabling the worker, as mt7915 does."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90367",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90367\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90367](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90367)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: hold dev-\u003emt76.mutex while disabling tx worker in SER\n\nmt7996_mac_reset_work() parked the tx worker and disabled the RX/TX NAPIs\nbefore taking dev-\u003emt76.mutex. mt76_worker_disable()/_enable() are plain\nkthread park/unpark, not refcounted, and __mt76_set_channel() toggles the\nsame worker and the MT76_RESET bit under the mutex. An L1 SER racing a\nchannel switch could therefore have the worker unparked and MT76_RESET\ncleared while the reset path resets the DMA rings, corrupting descriptors\nor tokens. Take the mutex before disabling the worker, as mt7915 does.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90367**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90367](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90367)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: hold dev-\u003emt76.mutex while disabling tx worker in SER\n\nmt7996_mac_reset_work() parked the tx worker and disabled the RX/TX NAPIs\nbefore taking dev-\u003emt76.mutex. mt76_worker_disable()/_enable() are plain\nkthread park/unpark, not refcounted, and __mt76_set_channel() toggles the\nsame worker and the MT76_RESET bit under the mutex. An L1 SER racing a\nchannel switch could therefore have the worker unparked and MT76_RESET\ncleared while the reset path resets the DMA rings, corrupting descriptors\nor tokens. Take the mutex before disabling the worker, as mt7915 does."
              },
              "properties": {
