            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97567",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: mptcp: prevent race between disconnect() and rtx"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: prevent race between disconnect() and rtx\n\nSashiko noted that the two event can race, leading to inconsistent\nstatus. Prevent the race using the synchronous timer stop operation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97567",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97567\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97567](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97567)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: prevent race between disconnect() and rtx\n\nSashiko noted that the two event can race, leading to inconsistent\nstatus. Prevent the race using the synchronous timer stop operation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97567**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97567](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97567)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: prevent race between disconnect() and rtx\n\nSashiko noted that the two event can race, leading to inconsistent\nstatus. Prevent the race using the synchronous timer stop operation."
              },
