            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98162",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: smb/server: fix tree connection leak in smb2_tree_connect()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/server: fix tree connection leak in smb2_tree_connect()\n\nSee the procedure below:\n\n  smb2_tree_connect\n    ksmbd_tree_conn_connect\n      xa_store(\u0026sess-\u003etree_conns, tree_conn-\u003eid, tree_conn)\n      ksmbd_counter_inc(KSMBD_COUNTER_TREE_CONNS)\n      ksmbd_share_tree_conn_inc(sc)\n    ksmbd_iov_pin_rsp // fail\n    status.ret = KSMBD_TREE_CONN_STATUS_NOMEM\n    // do not disconnect tree_conn\n\nDisconnect the new tree connection if ksmbd_iov_pin_rsp() fails."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98162",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98162\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98162](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98162)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/server: fix tree connection leak in smb2_tree_connect()\n\nSee the procedure below:\n\n  smb2_tree_connect\n    ksmbd_tree_conn_connect\n      xa_store(\u0026sess-\u003etree_conns, tree_conn-\u003eid, tree_conn)\n      ksmbd_counter_inc(KSMBD_COUNTER_TREE_CONNS)\n      ksmbd_share_tree_conn_inc(sc)\n    ksmbd_iov_pin_rsp // fail\n    status.ret = KSMBD_TREE_CONN_STATUS_NOMEM\n    // do not disconnect tree_conn\n\nDisconnect the new tree connection if ksmbd_iov_pin_rsp() fails.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98162**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98162](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98162)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/server: fix tree connection leak in smb2_tree_connect()\n\nSee the procedure below:\n\n  smb2_tree_connect\n    ksmbd_tree_conn_connect\n      xa_store(\u0026sess-\u003etree_conns, tree_conn-\u003eid, tree_conn)\n      ksmbd_counter_inc(KSMBD_COUNTER_TREE_CONNS)\n      ksmbd_share_tree_conn_inc(sc)\n    ksmbd_iov_pin_rsp // fail\n    status.ret = KSMBD_TREE_CONN_STATUS_NOMEM\n    // do not disconnect tree_conn\n\nDisconnect the new tree connection if ksmbd_iov_pin_rsp() fails."
              },
