            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98174",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  s ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix rlist race and missing initialization\n\nTCP_Server_Info.rlist is allocated via kzalloc which zeros both -\u003enext\nand -\u003eprev to NULL instead of pointing to itself, making list_empty()\nalways return false and list_add() dereference a NULL -\u003eprev pointer.\n\nAlso, cifs_signal_cifsd_for_reconnect() can be called concurrently\nfrom multiple cifsd threads, allowing the same server's rlist node to\nbe added twice into the local list, corrupting it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98174",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98174\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98174](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98174)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix rlist race and missing initialization\n\nTCP_Server_Info.rlist is allocated via kzalloc which zeros both -\u003enext\nand -\u003eprev to NULL instead of pointing to itself, making list_empty()\nalways return false and list_add() dereference a NULL -\u003eprev pointer.\n\nAlso, cifs_signal_cifsd_for_reconnect() can be called concurrently\nfrom multiple cifsd threads, allowing the same server's rlist node to\nbe added twice into the local list, corrupting it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98174**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98174](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98174)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix rlist race and missing initialization\n\nTCP_Server_Info.rlist is allocated via kzalloc which zeros both -\u003enext\nand -\u003eprev to NULL instead of pointing to itself, making list_empty()\nalways return false and list_add() dereference a NULL -\u003eprev pointer.\n\nAlso, cifs_signal_cifsd_for_reconnect() can be called concurrently\nfrom multiple cifsd threads, allowing the same server's rlist node to\nbe added twice into the local list, corrupting it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
