            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98179",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  d ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: fix rmmio iounmap skipped on device removal\n\namdgpu_pci_remove() calls drm_dev_unplug() before fini_sw(), so\ndrm_dev_enter() is already false there and the iounmap() guarded by it\nis skipped. This .remove path runs on both hot-unplug and plain rmmod,\nso the register BAR ioremap mapping leaks one instance per unload.\n\nUnmap rmmio unconditionally (guard only on non-NULL) and drop the now\nunused idx.\n\n(cherry picked from commit dd6f86a97260e5207d3329ad03aa89fdad61b1e6)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98179",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98179\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98179](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98179)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: fix rmmio iounmap skipped on device removal\n\namdgpu_pci_remove() calls drm_dev_unplug() before fini_sw(), so\ndrm_dev_enter() is already false there and the iounmap() guarded by it\nis skipped. This .remove path runs on both hot-unplug and plain rmmod,\nso the register BAR ioremap mapping leaks one instance per unload.\n\nUnmap rmmio unconditionally (guard only on non-NULL) and drop the now\nunused idx.\n\n(cherry picked from commit dd6f86a97260e5207d3329ad03aa89fdad61b1e6)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98179**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98179](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98179)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: fix rmmio iounmap skipped on device removal\n\namdgpu_pci_remove() calls drm_dev_unplug() before fini_sw(), so\ndrm_dev_enter() is already false there and the iounmap() guarded by it\nis skipped. This .remove path runs on both hot-unplug and plain rmmod,\nso the register BAR ioremap mapping leaks one instance per unload.\n\nUnmap rmmio unconditionally (guard only on non-NULL) and drop the now\nunused idx.\n\n(cherry picked from commit dd6f86a97260e5207d3329ad03aa89fdad61b1e6)"
              },
              "properties": {
