            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98194",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libertas_tf: fix UAF in lbtf_free_adapter()\n\nlbtf_free_adapter() calls lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() to free the command\nbuffers before calling timer_delete_sync() to wait for the command\ntimer callback.  If the timer callback (command_timer_fn) is already\nrunning when lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() frees the command array, the\ncallback dereferences priv-\u003ecur_cmd-\u003ecmdbuf which points to freed\nmemory.\n\nSwap the order so that timer_delete_sync() runs first, ensuring any\nin-flight callback has completed before the command buffers are freed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98194",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98194\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98194](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98194)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libertas_tf: fix UAF in lbtf_free_adapter()\n\nlbtf_free_adapter() calls lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() to free the command\nbuffers before calling timer_delete_sync() to wait for the command\ntimer callback.  If the timer callback (command_timer_fn) is already\nrunning when lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() frees the command array, the\ncallback dereferences priv-\u003ecur_cmd-\u003ecmdbuf which points to freed\nmemory.\n\nSwap the order so that timer_delete_sync() runs first, ensuring any\nin-flight callback has completed before the command buffers are freed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98194**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98194](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98194)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libertas_tf: fix UAF in lbtf_free_adapter()\n\nlbtf_free_adapter() calls lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() to free the command\nbuffers before calling timer_delete_sync() to wait for the command\ntimer callback.  If the timer callback (command_timer_fn) is already\nrunning when lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() frees the command array, the\ncallback dereferences priv-\u003ecur_cmd-\u003ecmdbuf which points to freed\nmemory.\n\nSwap the order so that timer_delete_sync() runs first, ensuring any\nin-flight callback has completed before the command buffers are freed."
              },
              "properties": {
