            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98195",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlegacy: fix broadcast stations deallocation\n\nOn the error path of __il4965_up(), il_dealloc_bcast_stations() clears\nonly IL_STA_UCODE_ACTIVE, leaving IL_STA_BCAST set. This causes the\nsame broadcast stations to be deallocated again by __il4965_down().\n\nThis can occur when RF_KILL is toggled during driver startup.\n\nTo fix clear the entire 'used' field, since we will not do any\nother operations on the station."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98195",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98195\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98195](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98195)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlegacy: fix broadcast stations deallocation\n\nOn the error path of __il4965_up(), il_dealloc_bcast_stations() clears\nonly IL_STA_UCODE_ACTIVE, leaving IL_STA_BCAST set. This causes the\nsame broadcast stations to be deallocated again by __il4965_down().\n\nThis can occur when RF_KILL is toggled during driver startup.\n\nTo fix clear the entire 'used' field, since we will not do any\nother operations on the station.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98195**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98195](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98195)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlegacy: fix broadcast stations deallocation\n\nOn the error path of __il4965_up(), il_dealloc_bcast_stations() clears\nonly IL_STA_UCODE_ACTIVE, leaving IL_STA_BCAST set. This causes the\nsame broadcast stations to be deallocated again by __il4965_down().\n\nThis can occur when RF_KILL is toggled during driver startup.\n\nTo fix clear the entire 'used' field, since we will not do any\nother operations on the station."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
