            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98285",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  n ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: vlan: fix bugs caused by switchdev deletion errors\n\nAllowing switchdev to prevent vlan deletion and error out in __vlan_del\ncould cause multiple different issues - inconsistent state, memory leaks\nwhen flushing, NULL pointer dereference on bridge error when flushing.\nIt doesn't make sense to allow it to stop __vlan_del, so log the error\nand continue with software vlan deletion. This is also consistent with\n8021q behaviour."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98285",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98285\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98285](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98285)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: vlan: fix bugs caused by switchdev deletion errors\n\nAllowing switchdev to prevent vlan deletion and error out in __vlan_del\ncould cause multiple different issues - inconsistent state, memory leaks\nwhen flushing, NULL pointer dereference on bridge error when flushing.\nIt doesn't make sense to allow it to stop __vlan_del, so log the error\nand continue with software vlan deletion. This is also consistent with\n8021q behaviour.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98285**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98285](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98285)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: vlan: fix bugs caused by switchdev deletion errors\n\nAllowing switchdev to prevent vlan deletion and error out in __vlan_del\ncould cause multiple different issues - inconsistent state, memory leaks\nwhen flushing, NULL pointer dereference on bridge error when flushing.\nIt doesn't make sense to allow it to stop __vlan_del, so log the error\nand continue with software vlan deletion. This is also consistent with\n8021q behaviour."
              },
