            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98291",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  B ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel_pcie: fix off-by-one bounds check in RX submit\n\nbtintel_pcie_submit_rx() used frbd_index \u003e rxq-\u003ecount to guard the\nFRBD array access, allowing frbd_index == rxq-\u003ecount to pass through\nand index one element past the end of the array. Change the check to\n\u003e= rxq-\u003ecount so every out-of-range index is rejected.\n\nThis issue was reported by Claude Mythos."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98291",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98291\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98291](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98291)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel_pcie: fix off-by-one bounds check in RX submit\n\nbtintel_pcie_submit_rx() used frbd_index \u003e rxq-\u003ecount to guard the\nFRBD array access, allowing frbd_index == rxq-\u003ecount to pass through\nand index one element past the end of the array. Change the check to\n\u003e= rxq-\u003ecount so every out-of-range index is rejected.\n\nThis issue was reported by Claude Mythos.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98291**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98291](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98291)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel_pcie: fix off-by-one bounds check in RX submit\n\nbtintel_pcie_submit_rx() used frbd_index \u003e rxq-\u003ecount to guard the\nFRBD array access, allowing frbd_index == rxq-\u003ecount to pass through\nand index one element past the end of the array. Change the check to\n\u003e= rxq-\u003ecount so every out-of-range index is rejected.\n\nThis issue was reported by Claude Mythos."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
