            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98308",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  A ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: hda: trace PCM open only after assigning a stream\n\nStream assignment can fail when hardware streams are exhausted.\nMove the tracepoint after the NULL check because its payload accesses\nthe assigned stream tag.\n\nDetected by static analysis and reviewed with AI-assisted source auditing."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98308",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98308\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98308)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: hda: trace PCM open only after assigning a stream\n\nStream assignment can fail when hardware streams are exhausted.\nMove the tracepoint after the NULL check because its payload accesses\nthe assigned stream tag.\n\nDetected by static analysis and reviewed with AI-assisted source auditing.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98308**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98308)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: hda: trace PCM open only after assigning a stream\n\nStream assignment can fail when hardware streams are exhausted.\nMove the tracepoint after the NULL check because its payload accesses\nthe assigned stream tag.\n\nDetected by static analysis and reviewed with AI-assisted source auditing."
