            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98325",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: set up the TX info early to fix failure paths\n\nThe previous commit 2c51457d930f (\"wifi: mac80211: free ack status\nframe on TX header build failure\") cleaned up the leak, but still\nleft the code a bit messy and the failed SKB didn't get reported\nto userspace.\n\nFix this up by initialising skb-\u003ecb[] earlier, which allows using\nieee80211_free_txskb() and therefore reports it for the failure\nin ieee80211_build_hdr(), and unifies the ieee80211_skb_resize()\nfailure path with it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98325",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98325\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98325](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98325)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: set up the TX info early to fix failure paths\n\nThe previous commit 2c51457d930f (\"wifi: mac80211: free ack status\nframe on TX header build failure\") cleaned up the leak, but still\nleft the code a bit messy and the failed SKB didn't get reported\nto userspace.\n\nFix this up by initialising skb-\u003ecb[] earlier, which allows using\nieee80211_free_txskb() and therefore reports it for the failure\nin ieee80211_build_hdr(), and unifies the ieee80211_skb_resize()\nfailure path with it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98325**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98325](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98325)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: set up the TX info early to fix failure paths\n\nThe previous commit 2c51457d930f (\"wifi: mac80211: free ack status\nframe on TX header build failure\") cleaned up the leak, but still\nleft the code a bit messy and the failed SKB didn't get reported\nto userspace.\n\nFix this up by initialising skb-\u003ecb[] earlier, which allows using\nieee80211_free_txskb() and therefore reports it for the failure\nin ieee80211_build_hdr(), and unifies the ieee80211_skb_resize()\nfailure path with it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98326",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: mesh: release the channel if start fails\n\nieee80211_join_mesh() acquires a channel context and then calls\nieee80211_start_mesh(), which can fail. In that case, the chanctx\nisn't released then interface removal will attempt to unassign it\nafter it's removed from the driver, hitting:\n\n  wlan0: Failed check-sdata-in-driver check, flags: 0x0\n  WARNING: net/mac80211/driver-ops.c:366 at drv_unassign_vif_chanctx\n   ieee80211_assign_link_chanctx\n   __ieee80211_link_release_channel\n   ieee80211_link_release_channel\n   ieee80211_teardown_sdata\n   unregister_netdevice_many_notify\n   _cfg80211_unregister_wdev\n   ieee80211_remove_interfaces\n   ieee80211_unregister_hw\n   mac80211_hwsim_del_radio\n   hwsim_exit_net\n\nCorrectly release the channel on start failures."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98326",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98326\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98326](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98326)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: mesh: release the channel if start fails\n\nieee80211_join_mesh() acquires a channel context and then calls\nieee80211_start_mesh(), which can fail. In that case, the chanctx\nisn't released then interface removal will attempt to unassign it\nafter it's removed from the driver, hitting:\n\n  wlan0: Failed check-sdata-in-driver check, flags: 0x0\n  WARNING: net/mac80211/driver-ops.c:366 at drv_unassign_vif_chanctx\n   ieee80211_assign_link_chanctx\n   __ieee80211_link_release_channel\n   ieee80211_link_release_channel\n   ieee80211_teardown_sdata\n   unregister_netdevice_many_notify\n   _cfg80211_unregister_wdev\n   ieee80211_remove_interfaces\n   ieee80211_unregister_hw\n   mac80211_hwsim_del_radio\n   hwsim_exit_net\n\nCorrectly release the channel on start failures.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98326**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98326](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98326)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: mesh: release the channel if start fails\n\nieee80211_join_mesh() acquires a channel context and then calls\nieee80211_start_mesh(), which can fail. In that case, the chanctx\nisn't released then interface removal will attempt to unassign it\nafter it's removed from the driver, hitting:\n\n  wlan0: Failed check-sdata-in-driver check, flags: 0x0\n  WARNING: net/mac80211/driver-ops.c:366 at drv_unassign_vif_chanctx\n   ieee80211_assign_link_chanctx\n   __ieee80211_link_release_channel\n   ieee80211_link_release_channel\n   ieee80211_teardown_sdata\n   unregister_netdevice_many_notify\n   _cfg80211_unregister_wdev\n   ieee80211_remove_interfaces\n   ieee80211_unregister_hw\n   mac80211_hwsim_del_radio\n   hwsim_exit_net\n\nCorrectly release the channel on start failures."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98327",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: mesh: reset the CSA state when leaving\n\nifmsh-\u003ecsa is allocated in ieee80211_mesh_csa_beacon() and only freed\nin ieee80211_mesh_finish_csa(), i.e. when the channel switch completes.\nLeaving the mesh while a switch is still pending therefore leaks it.\n\nAdditionally, ifmsh-\u003ecsa_role and ifmsh-\u003echsw_ttl have their state leak\nin this case, so things can get mixed up in addition to the memory\nleak.\n\nRefactor the reset and call it in ieee80211_stop_mesh() to fix it all."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98327",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98327\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98327](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98327)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: mesh: reset the CSA state when leaving\n\nifmsh-\u003ecsa is allocated in ieee80211_mesh_csa_beacon() and only freed\nin ieee80211_mesh_finish_csa(), i.e. when the channel switch completes.\nLeaving the mesh while a switch is still pending therefore leaks it.\n\nAdditionally, ifmsh-\u003ecsa_role and ifmsh-\u003echsw_ttl have their state leak\nin this case, so things can get mixed up in addition to the memory\nleak.\n\nRefactor the reset and call it in ieee80211_stop_mesh() to fix it all.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98327**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98327](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98327)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: mesh: reset the CSA state when leaving\n\nifmsh-\u003ecsa is allocated in ieee80211_mesh_csa_beacon() and only freed\nin ieee80211_mesh_finish_csa(), i.e. when the channel switch completes.\nLeaving the mesh while a switch is still pending therefore leaks it.\n\nAdditionally, ifmsh-\u003ecsa_role and ifmsh-\u003echsw_ttl have their state leak\nin this case, so things can get mixed up in addition to the memory\nleak.\n\nRefactor the reset and call it in ieee80211_stop_mesh() to fix it all."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98328",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: add HE 6 GHz capability in the scan elems len\n\nThe HE 6 GHz Band Capability element is in the probe request for\nevery band if 6 GHz is supported, so add the size to scan_ies_len.\n\nOtherwise, building probe request elements can fail, triggering the\nWARN_ON in __ieee80211_start_scan()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98328",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98328\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98328](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98328)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: add HE 6 GHz capability in the scan elems len\n\nThe HE 6 GHz Band Capability element is in the probe request for\nevery band if 6 GHz is supported, so add the size to scan_ies_len.\n\nOtherwise, building probe request elements can fail, triggering the\nWARN_ON in __ieee80211_start_scan().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98328**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98328](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98328)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: add HE 6 GHz capability in the scan elems len\n\nThe HE 6 GHz Band Capability element is in the probe request for\nevery band if 6 GHz is supported, so add the size to scan_ies_len.\n\nOtherwise, building probe request elements can fail, triggering the\nWARN_ON in __ieee80211_start_scan()."
              },
              "properties": {
