              "id": "CVE-2022-4543",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: KASLR Prefetch Bypass Breaks KPTI"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw named \"EntryBleed\" was found in the Linux Kernel Page Table Isolation (KPTI). This issue could allow a local attacker to leak KASLR base via prefetch side-channels based on TLB timing for Intel systems."
