              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68412",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68412\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-68412](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68412)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: cfg80211: Fix an error handling path in cfg80211_wext_siwscan()\n\nIf the test against IEEE80211_MAX_SSID_LEN fails, then 'creq' leaks.\nUse the existing error handling path to fix it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68412**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-68412](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68412)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: cfg80211: Fix an error handling path in cfg80211_wext_siwscan()\n\nIf the test against IEEE80211_MAX_SSID_LEN fails, then 'creq' leaks.\nUse the existing error handling path to fix it."
