            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46483",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "vim: command injection when decompressing .tgz archives"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to 9.2.0479, a command injection vulnerability exists in tar#Vimuntar() in\nruntime/autoload/tar.vim when decompressing .tgz archives on Unix-like systems. The function builds :!gunzip and :!gzip -d commands using shellescape(tartail) without the {special} flag, allowing a crafted archive filename to trigger Vim cmdline-special expansion and execute shell commands in the user's context. This vulnerability is fixed in 9.2.0479."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46483",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46483\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: vim-runtime\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-46483](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46483)\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to 9.2.0479, a command injection vulnerability exists in tar#Vimuntar() in\nruntime/autoload/tar.vim when decompressing .tgz archives on Unix-like systems. The function builds :!gunzip and :!gzip -d commands using shellescape(tartail) without the {special} flag, allowing a crafted archive filename to trigger Vim cmdline-special expansion and execute shell commands in the user's context. This vulnerability is fixed in 9.2.0479.",
