            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-52858",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "vim: Vim: Arbitrary code execution via Python omni-completion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to version 9.2.0561, the Python omni-completion script in python3complete.vim for Vim with the +python3 interpreter enabled (and the legacy pythoncomplete.vim for builds with the +python interpreter) executes the import and from statements found in the current buffer through Python's import machinery. Because the buffer's working directory is on sys.path, opening a hostile .py file with a sibling Python package and invoking omni-completion runs that package's top-level code as the editing user. This issue has been patched in version 9.2.0561."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-52858",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-52858\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: vim-runtime\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-52858](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-52858)\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to version 9.2.0561, the Python omni-completion script in python3complete.vim for Vim with the +python3 interpreter enabled (and the legacy pythoncomplete.vim for builds with the +python interpreter) executes the import and from statements found in the current buffer through Python's import machinery. Because the buffer's working directory is on sys.path, opening a hostile .py file with a sibling Python package and invoking omni-completion runs that package's top-level code as the editing user. This issue has been patched in version 9.2.0561.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-52858**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|vim-runtime||[CVE-2026-52858](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-52858)|\n\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to version 9.2.0561, the Python omni-completion script in python3complete.vim for Vim with the +python3 interpreter enabled (and the legacy pythoncomplete.vim for builds with the +python interpreter) executes the import and from statements found in the current buffer through Python's import machinery. Because the buffer's working directory is on sys.path, opening a hostile .py file with a sibling Python package and invoking omni-completion runs that package's top-level code as the editing user. This issue has been patched in version 9.2.0561."
              },
              "properties": {
