            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-73073",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "vim: Vim: Arbitrary command execution via crafted tags file in C omni-completion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to 9.2.0845, StructMembers() in runtime/autoload/ccomplete.vim constructs and executes a vimgrep command using an insufficiently escaped typeref: or typename: value from a tags file, allowing an unterminated collection followed by a command separator to execute arbitrary Ex and operating-system commands when a user invokes C omni-completion with CTRL-X CTRL-O on a member access whose type is resolved from that tags file. This issue is fixed in version 9.2.0845."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-73073",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-73073\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: vim-runtime\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-73073](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-73073)\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to 9.2.0845, StructMembers() in runtime/autoload/ccomplete.vim constructs and executes a vimgrep command using an insufficiently escaped typeref: or typename: value from a tags file, allowing an unterminated collection followed by a command separator to execute arbitrary Ex and operating-system commands when a user invokes C omni-completion with CTRL-X CTRL-O on a member access whose type is resolved from that tags file. This issue is fixed in version 9.2.0845.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-73073**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|vim-runtime||[CVE-2026-73073](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-73073)|\n\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to 9.2.0845, StructMembers() in runtime/autoload/ccomplete.vim constructs and executes a vimgrep command using an insufficiently escaped typeref: or typename: value from a tags file, allowing an unterminated collection followed by a command separator to execute arbitrary Ex and operating-system commands when a user invokes C omni-completion with CTRL-X CTRL-O on a member access whose type is resolved from that tags file. This issue is fixed in version 9.2.0845."
