                "text": "vim: Vim: Information disclosure via heap-based buffer overflow in Emacs-style tags file parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to version 9.2.0074, a heap-based buffer overflow out-of-bounds read exists in Vim's Emacs-style tags file parsing logic. When processing a malformed tags file, Vim can be tricked into reading up to 7 bytes beyond the allocated memory boundary. Version 9.2.0074 fixes the issue."
              },
