            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32249",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "vim: NFA regex engine NULL pointer dereference"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vim is an open source, command line text editor. From 9.1.0011 to before 9.2.0137, Vim's NFA regex compiler, when encountering a collection containing a combining character as the endpoint of a character range (e.g. [0-0\\u05bb]), incorrectly emits the composing bytes of that character as separate NFA states. This corrupts the NFA postfix stack, resulting in NFA_START_COLL having a NULL out1 pointer. When nfa_max_width() subsequently traverses the compiled NFA to estimate match width for the look-behind assertion, it dereferences state-\u003eout1-\u003eout without a NULL check, causing a segmentation fault. This vulnerability is fixed in 9.2.0137."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32249",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-32249\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: vim-runtime\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-32249](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32249)\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. From 9.1.0011 to before 9.2.0137, Vim's NFA regex compiler, when encountering a collection containing a combining character as the endpoint of a character range (e.g. [0-0\\u05bb]), incorrectly emits the composing bytes of that character as separate NFA states. This corrupts the NFA postfix stack, resulting in NFA_START_COLL having a NULL out1 pointer. When nfa_max_width() subsequently traverses the compiled NFA to estimate match width for the look-behind assertion, it dereferences state-\u003eout1-\u003eout without a NULL check, causing a segmentation fault. This vulnerability is fixed in 9.2.0137.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-32249**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|vim-runtime||[CVE-2026-32249](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32249)|\n\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. From 9.1.0011 to before 9.2.0137, Vim's NFA regex compiler, when encountering a collection containing a combining character as the endpoint of a character range (e.g. [0-0\\u05bb]), incorrectly emits the composing bytes of that character as separate NFA states. This corrupts the NFA postfix stack, resulting in NFA_START_COLL having a NULL out1 pointer. When nfa_max_width() subsequently traverses the compiled NFA to estimate match width for the look-behind assertion, it dereferences state-\u003eout1-\u003eout without a NULL check, causing a segmentation fault. This vulnerability is fixed in 9.2.0137."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
