              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-58470\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: wget\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-58470](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58470)\nGNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit 43d3ba9, contains an integer overflow vulnerability in the parse_content_range() function within src/http.c that allows server-controlled values to cause signed integer arithmetic to overflow. Attackers can supply malicious Content-Range header values to trigger undefined behavior and download desynchronization in the affected client.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-58470**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|wget||[CVE-2026-58470](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58470)|\n\nGNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit 43d3ba9, contains an integer overflow vulnerability in the parse_content_range() function within src/http.c that allows server-controlled values to cause signed integer arithmetic to overflow. Attackers can supply malicious Content-Range header values to trigger undefined behavior and download desynchronization in the affected client."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-16599",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "wget: wget: Denial of Service via crafted FTP OPIE/S-KEY authentication challenge"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU wget is vulnerable to denial of service in its FTP OPIE/S-KEY authentication functionality. The server-supplied sequence number from the FTP challenge line is used as an iteration count for an MD5 key-derivation loop without any upper bound validation. A malicious FTP server or a network attacker positioned to intercept FTP traffic can send a crafted OPIE challenge with a sequence number near INT_MAX, causing wget to perform up to approximately 2.1 billion MD5 computations and suspend for some time. The --timeout option does not mitigate this because it applies only to network I/O, not CPU computation.\n\n\nThis issue was fixed in commit e9697d98e7249b0f68a6be040a4f3dcc5bc101fa"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-16599",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-16599\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: wget\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-16599](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-16599)\nGNU wget is vulnerable to denial of service in its FTP OPIE/S-KEY authentication functionality. The server-supplied sequence number from the FTP challenge line is used as an iteration count for an MD5 key-derivation loop without any upper bound validation. A malicious FTP server or a network attacker positioned to intercept FTP traffic can send a crafted OPIE challenge with a sequence number near INT_MAX, causing wget to perform up to approximately 2.1 billion MD5 computations and suspend for some time. The --timeout option does not mitigate this because it applies only to network I/O, not CPU computation.\n\n\nThis issue was fixed in commit e9697d98e7249b0f68a6be040a4f3dcc5bc101fa",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-16599**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|wget||[CVE-2026-16599](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-16599)|\n\nGNU wget is vulnerable to denial of service in its FTP OPIE/S-KEY authentication functionality. The server-supplied sequence number from the FTP challenge line is used as an iteration count for an MD5 key-derivation loop without any upper bound validation. A malicious FTP server or a network attacker positioned to intercept FTP traffic can send a crafted OPIE challenge with a sequence number near INT_MAX, causing wget to perform up to approximately 2.1 billion MD5 computations and suspend for some time. The --timeout option does not mitigate this because it applies only to network I/O, not CPU computation.\n\n\nThis issue was fixed in commit e9697d98e7249b0f68a6be040a4f3dcc5bc101fa"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27171",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "zlib: zlib: Denial of Service via infinite loop in CRC32 combine functions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "zlib before 1.3.2 allows CPU consumption via crc32_combine64 and crc32_combine_gen64 because x2nmodp can do right shifts within a loop that has no termination condition."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27171",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-27171\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: zlib1g\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-27171](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27171)\nzlib before 1.3.2 allows CPU consumption via crc32_combine64 and crc32_combine_gen64 because x2nmodp can do right shifts within a loop that has no termination condition.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-27171**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|zlib1g||[CVE-2026-27171](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27171)|\n\nzlib before 1.3.2 allows CPU consumption via crc32_combine64 and crc32_combine_gen64 because x2nmodp can do right shifts within a loop that has no termination condition."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
